         I2.10    Plated structures

         I2.10.1 Plated structures are those stiffened plate elements in contact with the hull and
         subject to ice loads. These requirements are applicable to an inboard extent which is the
         lesser of:

              (i) web height of adjacent parallel web frame or stringer; or
              (ii) 2.5 times the depth of framing that intersects the plated structure

         I2.10.2 The thickness of the plating and the scantlings of attached stiffeners are to be such
         that the degree of end fixity necessary for the shell framing is ensured.

         I2.10.3 The stability of the plated structure is to adequately withstand the ice loads defined
         in I2.3.

